# Domain Modeling

- Use the ubiquitous language of the business in names (types, functions, events). Avoid generic names like `Manager`, `Data`, `Handler`.
- Model entities with identity and value objects without identity; make illegal states unrepresentable (union types, enums, constructors that validate).
- Business invariants live in the domain layer, not in controllers, UI, or SQL triggers.
- Money is integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. Never use floating point for money.
- Store and exchange timestamps in UTC (ISO 8601). Convert to local time only at the presentation edge.
- IDs are opaque strings (UUIDv7/ULID) generated by the system, never derived from user input.
- State transitions (orders, subscriptions, jobs) are explicit state machines with a single function per transition.
- Side effects (email, payments, webhooks) are triggered from the application layer via ports/interfaces, and must be idempotent.
- If a domain overlay file (`domain-*.mdc`) exists, follow it in addition to this rule.
